    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "623dd1dc_9b2ee935",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-17T04:37:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will call mNetworkRequests.clear(), which is sort of confusing to anyone trying to follow the tests. It means that mNetworkRequests doesn\u0027t contain all the requests, but only those requests that were added since the last expectAddRequests.\n\nIt\u0027s also not clear to me - why do we need the new mNetworkRequests list at all? NetworkFactory itself already has an mNetworkRequests member, can we simply just add a protected @VisibleForTesting accessor that can fetch that list (or a copy of it) and use that? The semantics are different in the sense that it\u0027s not ordered, but because it\u0027s keyed by request ID, we should be able to use it. If nothing else, maybe we can rely on the fact that CS assigns IDs consecutively, though that might be a terrible idea :)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3423,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 3423,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ceb4c452b78a09db4b326b7385913172f35f7fa1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc699266_400d4e3f",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3423,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-18T07:09:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not clearing anymore. Just tracking \u003d\u003d duplicating the code from NetworkFactory.\n\nExposing mNetworkRequests, whether as protected or through a @VisibleForTesting API, will both result in \"some\" network factory starting to use them directly to observe or manage the network request queue - as opposed to going through existing APIs. Both undesirable. A bit of code duplication isn\u0027t too much of a cost to avoid that.",
      "parentUuid": "623dd1dc_9b2ee935",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3423,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 3423,
